{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared vectors for where a ContextMenu's preview goes (CoreContextMenuPreview.place and",
    "CoreContextMenuContract.defaultPreviewGap).",
    "Read by coui_core ('cases': exact numbers in, exact box out), coui_flutter and coui_web",
    "('scenarios': a real menu opened at a pointer in a viewport of a given size, whose preview",
    "has to end up on the side the rule names, in the right place relative to the menu that",
    "was actually laid out) and a real-Chrome probe (the same scenarios on the compiled",
    "component). A change on one platform fails the others.",
    "",
    "The rule. A preview of natural size w x h goes around a menu inside a viewport. The sides are",
    "tried above, below, end, start; the first whose room holds the preview whole wins. If none does,",
    "the side with the most room wins (ties: the earlier side) and the preview is held to that room",
    "along that side's axis. Along its axis the preview sits `gap` from the menu; across it the",
    "preview's start edge lines up with the menu's start edge (above, below) or its top with the",
    "menu's top (end, start), then slides back inside the viewport. 'end' is right in 'ltr' and left",
    "in 'rtl'.",
    "",
    "All numbers are px; a box is [left, top, right, bottom], half-open; 'viewport' is the area the",
    "seat keeps panels inside (the window less the margin, the system bars and the keyboard).",
    "A case's 'expect.box' is the preview's box; 'capped' is whether it is smaller than the preview;",
    "'visible' is false when there is no room at all.",
    "",
    "A scenario opens a menu of 'rows' action rows at 'pointer' (viewport coordinates) in a viewport",
    "of 'viewport' = [width, height] with an 8 px margin and no system bars, shows a preview of",
    "'preview' = [width, height], and says which side of the menu it must land on ('side') and which",
    "physical side that is ('physical': above, below, left or right of the menu). Scenario answers",
    "hold for every menu 240 to 280 px wide and 110 to 140 px tall, the sizes a menu of three rows",
    "takes, because the seats lay out their own menus."
  ],
  "gap": 8,
  "cases": [
